course: dictionary
lesson: 12421
title: The dartboard
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dartboard is a round board, divided into numbered sections, that you throw darts at. The word is made of two parts, dart and board, so it names the board the darts are thrown at. «Dad hung the dartboard on the games room wall.» Here the dartboard is the round board on the wall.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Tom threw three darts at the dartboard.» Tom threw darts, so a dartboard must be the thing a dart is thrown at. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? A target fits, so a dartboard is a target for darts.
explain: Dartboards are found in pubs, games rooms and homes in the UK, Ireland, Australia and many other places. In maths, the dartboard gives you practice with adding, doubling and trebling. The outer ring doubles a score, the inner ring trebles it, and the centre is the bull's-eye.
fact: A dartboard is a round board, divided into numbered sections.
fact: You throw darts at a dartboard in the game of darts.
fact: «The dart hit the bull's-eye in the centre.» The bull's-eye is the middle of the dartboard.
fact: The outer ring of a dartboard doubles your score, and the inner ring trebles it.
fact: Darts are sharp, so only throw them when no one is near the dartboard.
exercise: «Dad hung the dartboard on the games room wall.» What is a dartboard? | *A round board with numbered sections, for throwing darts at | A board for writing sums in chalk | A sharp tool for cutting paper | A long wooden table for cards
exercise: In the game, which part of the dartboard doubles your score? | The inner ring | *The outer ring | The centre bull's-eye | The wall behind the board
exercise: «The dart hit the bull's-eye in the centre.» Which part of the dartboard is the centre? | The wall | The darts | *The bull's-eye | The outer ring
test: Why should you only throw darts when no one is near the dartboard? | The board needs quiet to work | Darts must be thrown at the wall first | *Darts are sharp and can hurt someone | Darts are light and float in the air
test: In maths practice, what does the inner ring of a dartboard do to a score? | It adds one to the score | It takes away five from the score | It halves the score | *It trebles the score
exam: «Tom threw three darts at the dartboard, and one hit the outer ring.» What does the outer ring do to the score? | It has no effect on the score | It trebles the score | *It doubles the score | It makes the score zero
